      "content": "I can't advise you to take medication without consulting your doctor. Serotonin syndrome is a rare but potentially life-threatening condition that can occur when certain medications, including tricyclic antidepressants like sertraline, interact with cough medications. However, the risk of serotonin syndrome is low, and your doctor can assess your individual situation and provide guidance on safe medication use. Considering your upcoming appointment, it's recommended to wait until then to consult with your doctor.",
